description:
The bridged token deployment script has no chain ID validation and names a hard-coded address as the timelock’s sole proposer and canceller; it does not set a timelock admin. It therefore produces identical governance wiring wherever it runs, unlike the canonical deployment script, which restricts itself to two Gensyn chain IDs.

Because `TimelockController` grants `DEFAULT_ADMIN_ROLE` only to itself when the admin argument is zero, deploying to a chain where that address cannot originate transactions yields a timelock whose proposer set cannot be repaired through its own role machinery: `MINTER_ROLE` and `BURNER_ROLE` never reach the bridge adapter, supply stays frozen at zero, and `_authorizeUpgrade` is unsatisfiable until the entire stack is redeployed.

That address is a three-of-five Safe address on the Ethereum mainnet holding neither `PROPOSER_ROLE` nor `CANCELLER_ROLE` on the live bridged timelock, and it has no code at all on Base, Arbitrum One, Optimism, or BSC. Therefore, the constant is not merely chain-dependent but also stale: production has already rotated governance away from it, so the next run of this script names a retired proposer on Ethereum as readily as on a chain the token has never reached.

```solidity
uint256 timelockMinDelay = 7 days;
address gensynSafeAddress = 0x90442673dae1b1572a3D994A4D795c8977A97ECD;
address[] memory timelockProposers = new address[](1);
timelockProposers[0] = gensynSafeAddress;
address[] memory timelockExecutors = new address[](1);
timelockExecutors[0] = address(0); // allow anyone to execute
address timelockAdmin = address(0); // renounce admin role to prevent centralization
address gensynTokenRecipient = 0x000000000000000000000000000000000000dEaD;
// Deploy Timelock
timelock = new TimelockController({
    minDelay: timelockMinDelay,
    proposers: timelockProposers,
    executors: timelockExecutors,
    admin: timelockAdmin
});
```

*Figure 2.1: The chain-independent proposer constant and the renounced timelock admin (`token/script/BridgedGensynToken.s.sol#L22–L39`)*

